        <guid>https://producthunt.programnotes.cn/en/p/bracket/</guid>
        <description>&lt;img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1673550632925-211ae506eb65?ixid=M3w0NjAwMjJ8MHwxfHJhbmRvbXx8fHx8fHx8fDE3NDY2ODkzMTF8&amp;ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Featured image of post bracket" /&gt;&lt;h1 id=&#34;evroonbracket&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/evroon/bracket&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;evroon/bracket&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img
    width=&#34;500&#34;
    src=&#34;frontend/public/favicon-wide.svg&#34;
    alt=&#34;Bracket - Tournament System&#34;
  /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/evroon/bracket/actions&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img
      src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/github/actions/workflow/status/evroon/bracket/backend.yml&#34;
      alt=&#34;build status&#34;
  /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://crowdin.com/project/bracket&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img
      src=&#34;https://badges.crowdin.net/bracket/localized.svg&#34;
      alt=&#34;translations&#34;
  /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/evroon/bracket/commits/&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img
      src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/github/last-commit/evroon/bracket&#34;
      alt=&#34;last commit&#34;
  /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/evroon/bracket/releases&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img
      src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/github/v/release/evroon/bracket&#34;
      alt=&#34;release&#34;
  /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://codecov.io/gh/evroon/bracket&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img
      src=&#34;https://codecov.io/gh/evroon/bracket/branch/master/graph/badge.svg?token=YJL0DVPFFG&#34;
      alt=&#34;codecov&#34;
  /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.bracketapp.nl/demo&#34;&gt;Demo&lt;/a&gt;
  ·
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl&#34;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;
  ·
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl/docs/running-bracket/quickstart&#34;&gt;Quickstart&lt;/a&gt;
  ·
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/evroon/bracket&#34;&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;
  ·
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/evroon/bracket/releases&#34;&gt;Releases&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tournament system meant to be easy to use. Bracket is written in async Python (with
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://fastapi.tiangolo.com&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;FastAPI&lt;/a&gt;) and &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://nextjs.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Next.js&lt;/a&gt; as frontend using the
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://mantine.dev/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Mantine&lt;/a&gt; library.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It has the following features:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports &lt;strong&gt;single elimination, round-robin and swiss&lt;/strong&gt; formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build your tournament structure&lt;/strong&gt; with multiple stages that can have multiple groups/brackets in
them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drag-and-drop matches&lt;/strong&gt; to different courts or reschedule them to another start time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Various &lt;strong&gt;dashboard pages&lt;/strong&gt; are available that can be presented to the public, customized with a
logo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create/update &lt;strong&gt;teams&lt;/strong&gt;, and add players to &lt;strong&gt;teams&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create &lt;strong&gt;multiple clubs&lt;/strong&gt;, with &lt;strong&gt;multiple tournaments&lt;/strong&gt; per club.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Swiss tournaments&lt;/strong&gt; can be handled dynamically, with automatic scheduling of matches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;img alt=&#34;&#34; src=&#34;docs/content/img/bracket-screenshot-design.png&#34; width=&#34;100%&#34; /&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
&lt;a href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explore the Bracket docs&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;▶&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;live-demo&#34;&gt;Live Demo
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;A demo is available for free at &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.bracketapp.nl/demo&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://www.bracketapp.nl/demo&lt;/a&gt;. The demo lasts for 30 minutes, after which
your data will de deleted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;quickstart&#34;&gt;Quickstart
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;To quickly run bracket to see how it works, clone it and run &lt;code&gt;docker compose up&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;git clone git@github.com:evroon/bracket.git
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; bracket
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo docker compose up -d
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This will start the backend and frontend of Bracket, as well as a postgres instance. You should now
be able to view bracket at http://localhost:3000. You can log in with the following credentials:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Username: &lt;code&gt;test@example.org&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Password: &lt;code&gt;aeGhoe1ahng2Aezai0Dei6Aih6dieHoo&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To insert dummy rows into the database, run:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo docker &lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;exec&lt;/span&gt; bracket-backend pipenv run ./cli.py create-dev-db
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;See also the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl/docs/running-bracket/quickstart&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;quickstart docs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;usage&#34;&gt;Usage
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Read the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl/docs/usage/guide&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;usage guide&lt;/a&gt; for how to organize a tournament in Bracket from start to finish.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;configuration&#34;&gt;Configuration
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Read the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl/docs/running-bracket/configuration&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;configuration docs&lt;/a&gt; for how to configure Bracket.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bracket&amp;rsquo;s backend is configured using &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt; files (&lt;code&gt;prod.env&lt;/code&gt; for production, &lt;code&gt;dev.env&lt;/code&gt; for development etc.).
But you can also configure Bracket using environment variables directly, for example by specifying them in the &lt;code&gt;docker-compose.yml&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The frontend doesn&amp;rsquo;t can be configured by environment variables as well, as well as &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt; files using Next.js&amp;rsquo; way of loading environment variables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;running-bracket-in-production&#34;&gt;Running Bracket in production
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Read the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl/docs/deployment&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;deployment docs&lt;/a&gt; for how to deploy Bracket and run it in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bracket can be run in Docker or by itself (using &lt;code&gt;pipenv&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;yarn&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;development-setup&#34;&gt;Development setup
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Read the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl/docs/community/development&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;development docs&lt;/a&gt; for how to run Bracket for development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prerequisites are &lt;code&gt;yarn&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;postgresql&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;pipenv&lt;/code&gt; to run the frontend, database and backend.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;translations&#34;&gt;Translations
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Based on your browser settings, your language should be automatically detected and loaded. For now,
there&amp;rsquo;s no manual way of choosing a different language.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;supported-languages&#34;&gt;Supported Languages
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;To add/refine translations, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://crowdin.com/project/bracket&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Crowdin&lt;/a&gt; is used.
See the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl/docs/community/contributing/#translating&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;docs&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;more-screenshots&#34;&gt;More screenshots
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;&#34; src=&#34;docs/content/img/schedule_preview.png&#34; width=&#34;50%&#34; /&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;&#34;
src=&#34;docs/content/img/planning_preview.png&#34; width=&#34;50%&#34; /&gt; &lt;img alt=&#34;&#34;
src=&#34;docs/content/img/builder_preview.png&#34; width=&#34;50%&#34; /&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;&#34;
src=&#34;docs/content/img/standings_preview.png&#34; width=&#34;50%&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;help&#34;&gt;Help
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;re having trouble getting Bracket up and running, or have a question about usage or configuration, feel free to ask.
The best place to do this is by creating a &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/evroon/bracket/discussions&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Discussion&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;supporting-bracket&#34;&gt;Supporting Bracket
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;re using Bracket and would like to help support its development, that would be greatly appreciated!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Several areas that we need a bit of help with at the moment are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⭐ &lt;strong&gt;Star Bracket&lt;/strong&gt; on GitHub&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌐 &lt;strong&gt;Translating&lt;/strong&gt;: Help make Bracket available to non-native English speakers by adding your language (via &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://crowdin.com/project/bracket&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;crowdin&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📣 &lt;strong&gt;Spread the word&lt;/strong&gt; by sharing Bracket to help new users discover it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🖥️ &lt;strong&gt;Submit a PR&lt;/strong&gt; to add a new feature, fix a bug, extend/update the docs or something else&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.bracketapp.nl/docs/community/contributing&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;contribution docs&lt;/a&gt; for more information on how to contribute&lt;/p&gt;
